==Specialty plates==
The first Conservation license plate featured a Salmon design. In 2009, New Brunswick introduced three new specialty license plate designs; Chickadee, Flower & Deer. The money earned from these plates go to the New Brunswick Wildlife Trust Fund.<ref>{{cite web |title=New conservation plates available |url=https://www1.gnb.ca/cnb/multimedia/display-e.asp?id=2087&num=1 |website=Communications New Brunswick |publisher=New Brunswick |access-date=10 August 2022}}</ref>
